From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:04:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] net: airoha: xpon: log the dying gasp after sending it

The dying-gasp handler printed its warning before queueing the PLOAM and
the OMCI dying gasp. On the 115200 baud console a line costs about
5 ms of the few the supply has left. Queue both messages first and log
afterwards, folding the "outside O5" note into the same line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 797424f..6c4e8bf 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -4293,16 +4293,19 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(gpon_dying_gasp_o5_only,
 static void gpon_handle_dying_gasp(struct xpon_priv *priv)
 {
 	enum gpon_state st = ploam_get_state(priv->ploam);
+	bool queued = false;
 	int ret;
 
-	dev_warn(priv->dev, "GPON dying-gasp interrupt in %s\n",
-		 gpon_state_name(st));
-	if (!READ_ONCE(gpon_dying_gasp_o5_only) || st == GPON_O5_OPERATION)
+	/* Queue both messages first; a console line costs milliseconds. */
+	if (!READ_ONCE(gpon_dying_gasp_o5_only) || st == GPON_O5_OPERATION) {
 		ploam_notify_dying_gasp(priv->ploam);
-	else
-		dev_warn_ratelimited(priv->dev,
-				     "GPON dying gasp outside O5: no Dying_Gasp PLOAM queued\n");
+		queued = true;
+	}
 	ret = airoha_gpon_omci_send_dying_gasp(&priv->omci);
+
+	dev_warn(priv->dev, "GPON dying-gasp interrupt in %s%s\n",
+		 gpon_state_name(st),
+		 queued ? "" : ": outside O5, no Dying_Gasp PLOAM queued");
 	if (ret && ret != -EOPNOTSUPP && ret != -ENOLINK)
 		dev_warn(priv->dev, "failed to send OMCI dying gasp: %d\n",
 			 ret);
